; worldenter.eval — in and out of a dungeon through the world map (P4).
;
; The round trip is the point: leave by the exit stair's route, enter by the
; location, and land back in the entry level. Two things it is really watching:
;
;   - `reset` must still leave the party in a LEVEL. A new game now opens on
;     the world map, so if reset ever inherits that, ten combat suites start
;     measuring a party standing in a field. The first `state`/`mapinfo` pair
;     is that check.
;   - an UNDISCOVERED location cannot be entered. The script discovers the
;     waystation explicitly, and the refusal before it is deliberate evidence
;     that discovery is a gate rather than decoration.
logecho on
reset
state
mapinfo

; --- out to the world -------------------------------------------------------
leave
state
world

; --- the gate: unknown places cannot be entered -----------------------------
enter waystation

; --- and once found, they can -----------------------------------------------
discover waystation
enter waystation
state
mapinfo
world
